CONCLUSION Part A: exact envelope == closed form C_N for all N=2..8: True
  (C_N: even N: min(2+4F,4); odd N=2M+1: 2+4F on [0,M/N], (6M+2)/N+2F on [M/N,(M+1)/N], then 4)
=== PART B: headline F*_os(N) = (sqrt(2)-1)/2 for all N>=2 ===
  Q(sqrt2) identity: 2 + 4*((sqrt2-1)/2) == 2*sqrt2:
    (Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(2, 1))   (expect (0,2));  equal: True
  N=2: first segment [0,1/2] contains F_os=(sqrt2-1)/2   [OK]
  N=3: first segment [0,1/3] contains F_os=(sqrt2-1)/2   [OK]
  N=4: first segment [0,1/2] contains F_os=(sqrt2-1)/2   [OK]
  N=5: first segment [0,2/5] contains F_os=(sqrt2-1)/2   [OK]
  N=6: first segment [0,1/2] contains F_os=(sqrt2-1)/2   [OK]
  N=7: first segment [0,3/7] contains F_os=(sqrt2-1)/2   [OK]
  N=8: first segment [0,1/2] contains F_os=(sqrt2-1)/2   [OK]
  Hence F*_os(N) = (sqrt2-1)/2 for every N>=2: PROVED (lower: Theorem OS-2; upper: Q*_N construction).
=== PART C: one-sided NS variant (Bob-side no-signalling) ===
--- C1: S_NS_os(2,F) = 2 for ALL F in [0,1/2] (exact) ---
  candidate affine functions S(F)=A+B*F collected: 640
  candidates exceeding 2 anywhere on [0,1/2]: 0
  S_NS_os(2,F) exact at F=0: 2; F=1/4: 2; F=1/2: 2
  CONCLUSION: S_NS_os(2,F) = 2 for ALL F in [0,1/2], exactly (one-sided NS is flat at N=2, like full NS Theorem 4).
--- C2: N=3 one-sided NS ---
  multisets with S_os_Q(F_os) = 2*sqrt(2) exactly: 12
    patterns [0, 0, 2] counts (c1,c2,c3,c4)=(2, 0, 1, 0)
    patterns [0, 0, 4] counts (c1,c2,c3,c4)=(2, 0, 1, 0)
    patterns [0, 1, 2] counts (c1,c2,c3,c4)=(2, 0, 1, 0)
    patterns [0, 1, 4] counts (c1,c2,c3,c4)=(2, 0, 1, 0)
    patterns [0, 2, 2] counts (c1,c2,c3,c4)=(1, 0, 2, 0)
    patterns [0, 2, 4] counts (c1,c2,c3,c4)=(1, 0, 2, 0)
    patterns [0, 4, 4] counts (c1,c2,c3,c4)=(1, 0, 2, 0)
    patterns [1, 1, 2] counts (c1,c2,c3,c4)=(2, 0, 1, 0)
    patterns [1, 1, 4] counts (c1,c2,c3,c4)=(2, 0, 1, 0)
    patterns [1, 2, 2] counts (c1,c2,c3,c4)=(1, 0, 2, 0)
    patterns [1, 2, 4] counts (c1,c2,c3,c4)=(1, 0, 2, 0)
    patterns [1, 4, 4] counts (c1,c2,c3,c4)=(1, 0, 2, 0)
  (all are exactly the round-robin types: two states of one row-type, one of the other)
  verifying the pinning identity exactly, per gauge:
  gauge check passed for all 96 (Q, gauge) pairs: NS forces w_L = 0, hence S = 2 identically under Bob-side NS
  CONCLUSION: every Q that reaches 2*sqrt(2) at F_os in the one-sided model has S = 2 IDENTICALLY under Bob-side NS. Hence
  S_NS_os(3, F_os) < 2*sqrt(2), i.e. F*_NS_os(3) > (sqrt2-1)/2: PROVED.
  (The exact vertex enumeration below strengthens this to full flatness.)
  exact vertex enumeration of {q0,q1 in Delta_3 : Bob-NS} per config:
  max S over all one-sided-NS models at N=3 with F = 2/3 (full simplex): 2   (expect exactly 2)
  CONCLUSION: S_NS_os(3,F) <= 2 for all F in [0,2/3] (monotonicity), and
  S = 2 is attained at F=0 by any local deterministic strategy, hence
  S_NS_os(3,F) = 2 for ALL F in [0,2/3]: PROVED. No Bell violation is
  possible at N=3 under one-sided NS at ANY fine-tuning level (the
  one-sided analog of Theorem 4; contrast full NS where F*_NS(3) =
  (sqrt2-1)/3, Theorem 5).
  LP cross-check: S_NS_os(3,0.000) = 2.000000000000
  LP cross-check: S_NS_os(3,0.100) = 2.000000000000
  LP cross-check: S_NS_os(3,0.200) = 2.000000000000
  LP cross-check: S_NS_os(3,0.300) = 2.000000000000
  LP cross-check: S_NS_os(3,0.400) = 2.000000000000
  LP cross-check: S_NS_os(3,0.500) = 2.000000000000
  LP cross-check: S_NS_os(3,0.600) = 2.000000000000
  LP cross-check: S_NS_os(3,0.660) = 2.000000000000
  LP cross-check: S_NS_os(3,0.667) = 2.000000000000
--- C3: explicit one-sided NS witnesses at F_os for N=4..8 (Q(sqrt2)) ---
  N=4: row sums 1: True; TV = F_os exactly: True; S = 2*sqrt(2): True; NS residuals 0: True; nonneg: True
  N=5: row sums 1: True; TV = F_os exactly: True; S = 2*sqrt(2): True; NS residuals 0: True; nonneg: True
  N=6: row sums 1: True; TV = F_os exactly: True; S = 2*sqrt(2): True; NS residuals 0: True; nonneg: True
  N=7: row sums 1: True; TV = F_os exactly: True; S = 2*sqrt(2): True; NS residuals 0: True; nonneg: True
  N=8: row sums 1: True; TV = F_os exactly: True; S = 2*sqrt(2): True; NS residuals 0: True; nonneg: True
  CONCLUSION: explicit algebraic one-sided NS witnesses at F_os exist for
  every N=4..8 (and the construction is general for all N>=4). With the
  lower bound S_NS_os <= S_os <= 2+4F (Theorem OS-2):
  F*_NS_os(N) = (sqrt2-1)/2 for all N>=4: PROVED.
