=== PART D: summary ===
OS-1 (row lemma, f in {-2,0,+2}^N): PROVED (report) + LP cross-checked (max dev 6.7e-16).
Theorem OS-2: S_os(N,F) <= 2+4F for all N>=2, F in [0,1]: PROVED (report; one-sided analog of S <= 2+8F).
Exact curves S_os_max(N,F) = C_N for N=2..8: PROVED (exact Fraction certificate, Part A). Even-N closed form min(2+4F,4): PROVED all N. Odd-N bend line: PROVED N=3,5,7; CONJECTURED for odd N>=9.
Cap F(S=4)_os(N) = ceil(N/2)/N: PROVED all N (concentration argument, report).
Headline: F*_os(N) = (sqrt2-1)/2 for all N>=2: PROVED. Flat in N from the start (no 4-saturation); equals the full-model F*(N=2).
One-sided NS: S_NS_os(2,F) = 2 for all F in [0,1/2]: PROVED (Part C1). S_NS_os(3,F) = 2 for all F in [0,2/3] (i.e. at ANY fine-tuning level):
PROVED (Part C2, exact vertex enumeration at F=2/3 = full simplex) — no
Bell violation possible at N=2 or N=3 under one-sided NS; contrast full
NS where F*_NS(3) = (sqrt2-1)/3 (Theorem 5). For N>=4:
F*_NS_os(N) = (sqrt2-1)/2: PROVED (Part C3 witnesses + Theorem OS-2).
Positioning vs Hall & Branciard 2020 (arXiv:2007.11903): their mutual-
information metric gives I_OS(SQ) ~ 0.128 bits vs I_C(SQ) ~ 0.080 bits (factor ~1.6, Eqs. 45/52); our TV metric gives factor exactly 2.
Orderings agree (one-sided costs more than full causal structure).
